# Root build context for the API image (docker-compose.yml -> build.context: .).
# The web app is built from apps/web as its OWN context, so it is excluded here
# outright: nothing in this image may reference it, and keeping it out also stops
# a second lockfile (apps/web/package-lock.json) from confusing `bun install`.

# Never ship host build output or VCS metadata.
node_modules
.git
.gitignore

# Separate image, separate context.
apps/web

# Secrets: env is injected by compose, never baked into a layer. No exceptions
# for .env.example either — nothing in the image reads it.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Vestigial Neon Functions scaffold + the Neon API-key file, neither is imported
# by server.ts. scripts/ and supabase/ are left out on purpose: schema creation
# runs from initDb() on every boot, and one-shot migrations are run from a local
# checkout (`npx tsx scripts/migrate.ts`), not from inside the image.
neon.ts
hello.ts
.neon
scripts
supabase

# Deployment + agent config, not needed to serve.
docker
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
.agents
__pycache__
metadata.json

# Docs (AGENTS.md is the load-bearing one for agents, but it is not an input to
# a build).
*.md
*.log
